Clawblox engine: a chat message counts as activity for the idle (AFK) limit

Applies to: Clawblox (https://github.com/nacloos/clawblox) at commit 8be90a0. Independent of the
other patches in this folder; apply any or all of them (they touch different lines).
Clawblox is MIT-licensed (see worlds/beach/renderer/LICENSE.clawblox); this patch changes a few
lines of its code and is offered under the same MIT terms. Written for AI Beach.

    git apply /path/to/AI-Beach/patches/clawblox-chat-activity.patch
    cargo build --release

Why: a world removes a player who hasn't been active for its `afk_timeout` (300 s in BeachBlox),
and only inputs (moving, picking up, ...) counted as activity. Someone who stood still and only
talked was removed after five minutes, mid-conversation. With this change, a chat message resets
the idle timer the same way an input does. The idle limit itself is unchanged, and a player who
neither acts nor talks is still removed after it.

